<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP MEDAL ROUND RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP MEDAL ROUND RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results in the world ice hockey</p>
<p>championship medal round on Friday:</p>
<p> Canada   2   Russia   1   (1-0 0-1 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Canada - Keith Primeau (14:18), Travis Green (46:26).</p>
<p>Russia - Vyacheslav Butsayev (31:33).</p>
<p>Penalties: Canada 10 minutes, Russia 10 minutes.</p>
<p>Attendance: 13,147</p>
<p>Canada play Sweden in the best-of-three world championshp</p>
<p>final starting on Sunday.</p>
<p>   United States 0 Finland 2 (0-0 0-1 0-1)   </p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Finland - Antti Aalto (22:47), Teppo Numminen (40:49).</p>
<p>Penalties: United States 8 minutes, Finland 6 minutes and</p>
<p>Petteri Nummelin 10 min (misconduct).</p>
<p>Attendance: 13,230</p>
<p>Final standings:</p>
<p>			   P   W  D  L   F   A   Pts</p>
<p> 1. Sweden	     5   4  0  1  17   9    8</p>
<p> 2. Canada	     5   3  0  2  13  14    6</p>
<p> 3. Russia	     5   2  1  2  13  13    5</p>
<p> 4. Czech Republic   5   2  0  3  12  12    4</p>
<p> 5. Finland	    5   2  0  3  12  12    4</p>
<p> 6. United States    5   1  1  3   7  14    3</p>
<p>Sweden and Canada meet in the best-of-three final, starting</p>
<p>on Sunday. The second final will be played on Tuesday  and, if</p>
<p>necessary, a third final on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Russia and the Czech Republic meet in the one-off bronze</p>
<p>final on Saturday.</p>
</text>
